    "case_id": "miracl-zh-91294#0",
    "historical_answer": "Based on the provided reference materials, Sagittarius (人马座) is bordered by the following neighboring constellations:\n\n*   **Scorpio**: Located to the west (西接天蝎座).\n*   **Aquarius**: Located to the east (東連摩羯座). *Note: The text contains a typo, stating \"Aquarius\" (摩羯座) instead of the correct \"Aquarius\" (寶瓶座) for the constellation east of Sagittarius.*\n*   **Ophiuchus**: Located to the north (北面是蛇夫座).\n*   **Scutum**: Located to the north (盾牌座).\n*   **Ophiuchus**: The text also mentions \"巨蛇座\" (Ophiuchus) as being to the north.\n*   **Telescopium**: Located to the south (望远镜座).\n*   **Microscopium**: Located to the south (显微镜座).\n*   **Corona Australis**: Located to the south (南冕座).\n\nThe materials indicate that Sagittarius is one of the largest and most prominent constellations in the summer night sky.",
